{"id":"h042","run":2,"role":"test_right","category":"science-chemistry","question":"The yellow light of a sodium lamp has an average wavelength of 5890 \\AA. Calculate the energy in (a) electron volts and (b) kilocalories per mole.\nIs the correct answer \"(a) 2.8eV and (b) 64.7 Kcal/mole\"?","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":"TIGER-Lab/MMLU-Pro, test split","claims":[{"text":"The proposed answer (2.8 eV and 64.7 kcal/mol) is incorrect in both parts.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Photon energy is given by E = hc/λ with hc ≈ 1239.8 eV·nm.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-0.3,"theta":1.5237,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"5890 Å equals 589.0 nm.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-0.2,"theta":1.5237,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The energy of the 5890 Å photon is about 2.10 eV.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The proposed 2.8 eV is wrong.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"1 eV corresponds to about 23.06 kcal/mol.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.3,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The energy is about 48.5 kcal/mol.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The proposed 64.7 kcal/mol is wrong, and the error carries over from part (a), since 64.7 corresponds to about 2.8 eV.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The physics is unambiguous and the calculation is direct.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-0.5,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"A different value of hc or of the eV-to-kcal/mol factor could change the answer, but not enough to explain a discrepancy this large.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-0.8,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":3,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":4,"J":0.95,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":6,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":9,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":3,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":4,"J